/-!
# Immersions with an exact and locally split conormal sequence

For immersions `i : Z ⟶ Y` and `j : Y ⟶ X` the conormal sequence of [Stacks Project, Tag 062S]
is `i^* 𝒞_{Y/X} ⟶ 𝒞_{Z/X} ⟶ 𝒞_{Z/Y} ⟶ 0`.  This file records what it means for that sequence
to be exact and locally split, the hypothesis under which regularity of `i ≫ j` descends to `i`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.exists_adapted_local_generators`: near `x = j (i z)` the ideal of `Y`
  is generated by sections whose classes are a basis of `I_x / 𝔪_x I_x` and extend to a basis of
  `J_x / 𝔪_x J_x`, the local-generators step in the proof of [Stacks Project, Tag 068Z].
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.exists_adapted_cotangent_bases`: the same pair of adapted bases of the
  cotangent fibres at `x`, available whenever an element of `I_x` lying in `𝔪_x J_x` already lies
  in `𝔪_x I_x`, which by
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.mk_eq_zero_of_mk_eq_zero_of_retraction` holds as soon as `j` admits a
  retraction.

## Implementation notes

Finite generation of the ideal of `Y` at `x` comes from [Stacks Project, Tag 01TV] read on an
affine open `V` inside the coborder of the range of `j`:  over `V` the morphism `j` restricts to
a closed immersion, which is affine and hence quasi-compact, so finite presentation makes the
kernel of its map on sections finitely generated.  That kernel is the ideal sheaf of the
restriction, which is the restriction of the ideal sheaf of `j`, so those finitely many sections
generate the latter on `V` and in particular generate its stalk at `x`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.22.8 (Tag 068Z)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/068Z)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 29.21.7 (Tag 01TV)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01TV)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 10.20.1 (Tag 00DV)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00DV)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

